{#-
  The house's models of the person living in it, the parts that are about a house rather than control in general
  (that's control.jinja). packages/estimates.yaml runs them. docs/control.md explains the model.
-#}

{#- Asleep, one minute of the filter (a two-state hidden Markov model run forward).

    The clock and the context don't count as evidence each minute, they set the chance of falling
    asleep in this minute (the hazard). Evidence that repeats every minute (the phone on the charger,
    the house in Night) would otherwise add up minute after minute and get very sure of itself, which
    is the naive Bayes trap the old sensor fell into. The only per-minute evidence is something
    happening: a sign of life since the last update is twenty times likelier awake, typing at the
    computer a thousand times. "Since the last update" rather than "in the last 60 seconds", so one
    landing exactly on a tick, or a late tick, still counts once.

    Returns JSON: b (the new belief), enter and wake (this minute's hazards), ratio (the evidence),
    quiet (minutes since the last sign of life), at (when this update ran) -#}
{%- macro asleep_next() -%}
{%- from 'control.jinja' import param, bayes_step -%}
{%- set prev = (states('sensor.asleep_belief') | float(5)) / 100 -%}
{%- set h = now().hour -%}
{%- set base = param('asleep_hazard_late') | float if (h >= 23 or h < 4)
               else (param('asleep_hazard_evening') | float if h >= 21
               else (param('asleep_hazard_early') | float if h < 7
               else param('asleep_hazard_day') | float)) -%}
{%- set life = states('sensor.last_sign_of_life') | as_datetime(none) -%}
{%- set quiet = ((now() - life).total_seconds() / 60) if life is not none else 999 -%}
{%- set last_at = (state_attr('sensor.asleep_belief', 'model') or {}).get('at', now().timestamp() - 60) | float -%}
{%- set active = life is not none and life.timestamp() >= last_at -%}
{%- set lights_on = expand(label_entities('light_ambient') + label_entities('light_task'))
                    | selectattr('state', 'eq', 'on') | list | count > 0 -%}
{%- set typing = is_state('binary_sensor.at_the_desk', 'on') -%}
{%- set home = is_state('person.resident', 'home') or is_state('binary_sensor.phone_on_home_wifi', 'on')
               or not is_state('input_select.house_mode', 'Away') -%}
{%- set m = (3 if is_state('input_select.house_mode', 'Night') else 1)
          * (1 if lights_on else 2)
          * (6 if quiet >= 45 else (3 if quiet >= 15 else 1))
          * (1.5 if is_state('input_boolean.phone_on_charger', 'on') else 1)
          * (1.3 if is_state('binary_sensor.phone_focus', 'on') else 1)
          * (0.5 if is_state('binary_sensor.tv_picture', 'on') else 1)
          * (1.5 if is_state('binary_sensor.bedroom_door', 'off') and (h >= 21 or h < 6) else 1) -%}
{%- set enter = 0 if typing else [base * m, param('asleep_hazard_max') | float] | min -%}
{%- set wake = param('asleep_wake_hazard') | float * (4 if 5 <= h < 11 else 1)
             * (5 if is_state('input_boolean.waking_up', 'on') else 1) -%}
{%- set ratio = param('asleep_typing_ratio') | float if typing
                else (param('asleep_activity_ratio') | float if active else 1) -%}
{#- never surer than 99%: from 99.99 a three-minute trip to the bathroom couldn't pull it back -#}
{%- set b = 0.0001 if not home else [bayes_step(prev, 1 - wake, enter, ratio) | float, param('asleep_max') | float] | min -%}
{{- {'b': b, 'enter': enter | round(5), 'wake': wake | round(5), 'ratio': ratio, 'quiet': quiet | round(0) | int, 'at': now().timestamp() | round(1)} | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}

{#- Someone home, from the front door and what moves inside, phone or no phone: the "wasp in a box".
    A person can't get in or out without the door, so:
      door closes                    -> checking: is anyone still in there?
      anything inside moves after it -> in, and in stays in until the door opens again (sitting
                                        still in the bedroom for an hour doesn't make the house empty)
      nothing inside for N minutes   -> out
    "Inside" is the Hub seeing someone (not while the robot vacuum's out or just back), a light changed
    by hand, the TV coming on, typing at the computer, someone talking to Jarvis, "I'm up".
    kind is what just happened, label says what it was, for the record.
    Returns JSON: phase (in, checking, out, unknown), door_closed_at and last_inside (epoch
    seconds), why -#}
{%- macro occupancy_next(kind, label='') -%}
{%- from 'control.jinja' import param -%}
{%- set t = now().timestamp() -%}
{%- set me = 'binary_sensor.someone_home' -%}
{%- set phase = state_attr(me, 'phase') or 'unknown' -%}
{%- set closed = state_attr(me, 'door_closed_at') | float(0) -%}
{%- set inside = state_attr(me, 'last_inside') | float(0) -%}
{%- set why = state_attr(me, 'why') or '' -%}
{%- set vac = states.vacuum.robot_vacuum -%}
{#- (just back counts for five minutes, but not a restart making it look just changed) -#}
{%- set started = (states('sensor.home_assistant_started') | as_datetime(now() - timedelta(hours=1))) + timedelta(seconds=60) -%}
{%- set vacuum_about = vac is not none and (vac.state in ['cleaning', 'returning', 'paused']
                       or ((now() - vac.last_changed).total_seconds() < 300 and vac.last_changed > started)) -%}
{%- if kind == 'door_close' -%}
  {%- set phase, closed, why = 'checking', t, 'the door closed, waiting to see if anyone moves inside' -%}
{%- elif kind == 'inside' and not (label == 'the Hub saw someone' and vacuum_about) -%}
  {%- set phase, inside, why = 'in', t, label -%}
{%- elif kind == 'tick' and phase == 'checking' and t - closed > (param('empty_after_door_minutes') | float) * 60 -%}
  {%- set phase, why = 'out', 'nobody moved inside for ' ~ param('empty_after_door_minutes') ~ ' minutes after the door closed' -%}
{%- endif -%}
{{- {'phase': phase, 'door_closed_at': closed | round(0), 'last_inside': inside | round(0), 'why': why} | to_json -}}
{%- endmacro -%}
